  "checks": [
    "The exact physical scaling is g_epsilon(x)=g(epsilon*x). The chain rule gives Delta g_epsilon=epsilon^2 Delta g(epsilon*x), and positive-scale Coulomb homogeneity gives V(epsilon*x)=epsilon^(-1)V(x). Therefore Delta g_epsilon=2(epsilon*V-epsilon^2*E)g_epsilon, scaling both attraction and repulsion.",
    "collisionFree_real_smul uses the nonzero-scale hypothesis to preserve every nuclear and pair noncollision. The physical homogeneity/application theorem correctly assumes epsilon>0. Classical smoothness is only invoked at genuinely collision-free points.",
    "The fixed nuclear chart yields principal c=4 and coefficient 8||y||^2(epsilon*V-epsilon^2*E). The unscaled physical-center pair chart yields c=1 and coefficient 4||y||^2(epsilon*V-epsilon^2*E). The KS chart coordinates themselves are fixed while all physical coordinates are dilated.",
    "Classical-to-weak application discharges its actual principal equation and local smoothness hypotheses using off-zero coefficient patches. The weak extension across y=0 uses continuity of the same physical representative and smoothness of the epsilon coefficient on the fixed open patch. Final integrability is supplied by removability; it is not inferred from a totalized divergent integral.",
    "originScaledDifference is exactly epsilon^(-1)*(g(epsilon*x)-g(0)). The forcing application uses b=P(Z,epsilon*E) and coefficient epsilon*b. Its source is -P(Z,epsilon*E)*g(0), with no inverse epsilon; both operator-test and source-test integrabilities are conclusions.",
    "At the selected collision the difference source is +8*Z*g(0) in a nuclear chart and -4*g(0) in the pair chart. These signs follow from the negative nuclear and positive repulsive pair constants.",
    "Each full-spin theorem chooses one simultaneous locally Lipschitz representative family before quantifying over every spin component, positive epsilon, chart and test. Its common almost-everywhere set and simultaneous spatial/spin permutation identity are retained.",
    "Physical final statements assume the actual Hamiltonian eigen-graph. They do not assume the new weak equations or derivatives of the scaled difference. Continuous representatives, rather than arbitrary L2 equivalence classes, are composed with KS maps.",
    "All nine current source/object hashes equal the four strict receipts. All 28 expanded types and transitive standard-three axiom reports occur in exact declared order, with zero printer ellipses."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This unit gives physical scaled weak equations and exact normalized-difference forcing, not a uniform derivative estimate or analytic/approximation rate.",
    "Pair statements are for N=2. Nuclear scalar statements allow arbitrary N with a selected electron, but the simultaneous full-spin wrappers here are N=2.",
    "Each chart retains its stated coefficient patch; excluded simultaneous collision strata are not silently covered.",
    "The eigen-graph is conditional input. No ground-state existence, uniqueness, gap, binding or full Theorem T conclusion follows from this unit alone."
  ],
